**2/**
About half of each 3.3 ms decode step is spent waiting between dependent steps (~{{ (K.fixed4_ms*1000/43)|n(0) }} µs per transformer block), not moving weights.

That's why 8 GPUs are only {{ K.tp8_gain|pct }} faster per step than 4: more GPUs speed up the streaming, not the waiting.

📎 `results/fig_strong_scaling.png`

![Strong scaling](results/fig_strong_scaling.png)

**3/**
Win #1 needs no new hardware. Run the model as one persistent program with flag hand-offs, and stream the next layers' weights while this layer's experts load.

Same 4x GB300, modeled: {{ C.gpu_df_tp4.tok_s_user|n }} tok/s/user, {{ K.sw_vs_meas|x }} today.

